To create a web page that displays an image with a caption underneath it using HTML and CSS, follow these steps:

1. Create a new HTML document (you can use any text editor like Notepad, Sublime Text, or Visual Studio Code). Save the file as `index.html`.

2. Add the following HTML code inside the body tag:

```html
<div id="img-container">
  <a href="http://www.example.com"><img src="image.jpg" alt="Image"></a>
  <p>Caption goes here</p>
</div>
```

Let's break down what's happening here:

- We start by creating a div element with an ID of `img-container`. This will be used to position our image and caption.
- Inside the `img-container`, we add an anchor (a) tag which is used to create a hyperlink. The href attribute specifies the URL that the link will go to.
- Inside the anchor tag, we add an img tag which is used to display the image. The src attribute specifies the location of the image, and the alt attribute provides alternative text for the image.
- After the image tag, we add a paragraph (p) tag which will contain the caption.

3. Next, let's add some styling using CSS. You can either include the styles inside your HTML file (inside the head tag), or create a separate CSS file and link it to your HTML file. For simplicity, let's add the styles inside the head tag.

```css
#img-container {
  text-align: center;
}

#img-container img {
  max-width: 100%;
  height: auto;
}

#img-container p {
  margin: 0;
  font-style: italic;
}
