```js
const diff = '- Array []\n'+
              '+\n'+
              '+\n'+
              '+\n'+
              '+\n'+
              '+\n'+
              '+\n';

// Remove leading and trailing whitespace
diff = diff.replace(/^[\s\r\n]+/, '').replace(/[\s\r\n]+$/, '');

// Split by newline characters
const lines = diff.split('\n');

// Filter out empty lines
const nonEmptyLines = lines.filter(line => line.trim() !== '');

// Parse each non-empty line as an addition or removal
const additions = [];
const removals = [];

nonEmptyLines.forEach(line => {
  const sign = line[0];
  const value = line.slice(2).trim();

  if (sign === '+' || sign === ' ') {
    // If the line starts with a plus sign or space, it's an addition
    additions.push(value);
  } else if (sign === '-') {
    // If the line starts with a minus sign, it's a removal
    removals.push(value);
  }
});

// Flatten arrays of additions and removals
const changes = [...additions, ...removals].flat();

// Convert string values to appropriate data types
const parsedChanges = changes.map(change => {
  let result;
  try {
    result = JSON.parse(change);
    return result;
  } catch (error) {}
  return change;
});

// Return final array of changes
return parsedChanges;
```

In this code, we first remove any leading/trailing whitespace from the Jest diff. We then split the diff by newline characters, filter out empty lines, and parse each non-empty line as an addition or removal based on the sign character at the beginning of the line. Finally, we flatten the arrays of additions and removals and map each change to its appropriate data type (either a primitive value or a nested object). The resulting array is returned at the end. This implementation

